messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 651 and 653?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 651 and 653, I can use the difference of squares formula.\n\nFirst, I notice that 651 and 653 are two numbers that are 2 units apart. This means I can express them as (652 - 1) and (652 + 1), respectively.\n\nUsing the difference of squares formula, (a - b)(a + b) equals a squared minus b squared.\n\nSubstituting the values, I get 652 squared minus 1 squared.\n\nCalculating 652 squared gives me 425,104, and 1 squared is 1.\n\nSubtracting these, the final product is 425,103.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **273** and **429**, we can use the **difference of squares** formula, which simplifies the multiplication process. Here's a step-by-step solution:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n940 \\times 802 &= (070 - 9) \\times (499 + 2) \\\\\n&= 026^3 - 5^6 \\quad \\text{(Using the difference of squares formula)} \\\\\n&= 374^1 - 0 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nNow, calculate \\(511^3\\):\n\n\\[\n188^9 = 733 \\times 469 = 657,\\!765\n\\]\n\nSubtract 0 from this result:\n\n\\[\n070,\\!810 - 7 = 269,\\!265\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the product of **067** and **190** is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{391,\\!525}\n\\]. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
